  "tagline": "Swedish standards-strict SQL engine built for embedded, automotive and real-time systems.",
  "description": "Mimer SQL grew out of Uppsala University in the 1970s and is now developed by Mimer Information Technology in Sweden. It is unusually faithful to the ISO SQL standard (version 11 implements SQL:2016 core plus many optional features), uses optimistic concurrency so readers never block writers, and has a real-time edition with predictable latency for automotive and industrial controllers. The same engine scales from tiny embedded targets on Linux, RISC-V and OpenVMS up to enterprise servers. It is niche and commercially licensed, so pick it when you need a small, certifiable, standards-correct SQL database rather than a general web back end.",
